#: includes/options-page.php:184
msgid "Auto Resize"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:192
msgid "When enabled, images use a placeholder and Gumlet.js resizes per viewport (including lazy loading, if enabled). When disabled, Gumlet.js is not loaded: the image src is set directly to the Gumlet URL (no placeholder and no lazy loading)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:193
msgid "Ignored while Signed URLs is enabled under Experimental. Auto Resize stays off so Gumlet.js cannot change a URL after it is signed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:199
msgid "Use Original Images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:206
msgid "If this is enabled (recommended), plugin will use original images before processing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:206
msgid "If this is not enabled, Gumlet will use images resized by wordpress for further processing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:212
msgid "Browser Webp Detect"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:219
msgid "If this is enabled, plugin will detect Webp support from browser rather than from server.(recommended OFF)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:225
msgid "Use <img> Width"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:231
msgid "If this is enabled, plugin will use width from <img> element width attribute rather than calculating actual width."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:237
msgid "Use Flex Width"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:243
msgid "If this is enabled, plugin will use width from Flex CSS property rather than calculating actual width."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:249
msgid "Minimum Width"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:254
msgid "If set, this will be minimum pixel width for image serving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:260
msgid "Exclude Image URLs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:265
msgid "Enter every URL in new line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:267
msgid "The URLs you enter here will not be processed by Gumlet. Please enter one URL per line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:273
msgid "Exclude Post Types"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:278
msgid "Enter each post type in new line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:280
msgid "Enter post types here to exclude those posts from being processed with Gumlet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:287
msgid "Experimental"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:294
msgid "Optimize Priority Images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:301
msgid "Serves your most important image (usually the hero or first image) through Gumlet at the right size for each screen, without waiting for Gumlet.js. WordPress and many themes mark this image with fetchpriority=\"high\", and by default Gumlet leaves it untouched, so it loads at its full original size."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:302
msgid "Turn this on to improve Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) and reduce mobile page weight. Recommended if your theme uses large banner or slider images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:308
msgid "Aspect-Ratio Placeholders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:315
msgid "While an image is waiting to load, reserves space with the image's exact shape (from its width and height attributes) instead of a 1x1 square. This stops content from jumping as images load (better CLS) and fixes gaps in masonry grids, galleries and sliders that measure images while loading. Images without width and height use the default placeholder."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:316
msgid "Turn this on if you see large gaps or overlapping content that corrects itself when the browser window is resized."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:322
msgid "Signed URLs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:329
msgid "Signs each image URL with your Gumlet source secure token. Unsigned or modified URLs are rejected, which stops other sites from using your images or CDN and consuming bandwidth."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:330
msgid "Auto Resize will not run while this is on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:330
msgid "Gumlet.js adds the width in the browser after the URL is signed, and Gumlet rejects the changed URL. Images are served from the signed URL directly. Gumlet.js lazy loading stays off as well. In the Gumlet dashboard, open the image source, Security tab, and turn on Secure URLs. Paste the token below and save here before enabling it on the source, then clear any page cache."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:336
msgid "Secure token"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:343
msgid "From the source Security tab. Used only on the server to sign URLs. Leave Signed URLs off until this is saved."
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:349
msgid "Expiry (seconds)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:354
msgid "Optional"
msgstr ""

#: includes/options-page.php:357
msgid "Optional. Leave blank and signed URLs do not expire. A number is how many seconds the URL stays valid after the page is rendered (3600 is one hour). Gumlet rejects it after that and caches the image only until then. Keep any full-page cache shorter than this value."
msgstr ""

